---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /developers/voiceml/
title: "VoiceML for developers"
description: "VoiceTel's XML-based voice runtime for teams that already use voice markup, callbacks, recordings, conferences, queues, and API-driven call flows. Move the economics without rewriting call logic."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Developers · VoiceML</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Move programmable voice workloads without rewriting call logic.</h1>
			<p class="lede">VoiceML is VoiceTel's XML-based voice runtime for teams that already use voice markup, callbacks, recordings, conferences, queues, and API-driven call flows. Preserve the interaction model you built while moving the economics, support path, and carrier layer to VoiceTel.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/signup/">Start building {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="/voiceml/">VoiceML overview</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set code %}{% highlight "xml" %}<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Response>
  <Gather numDigits="1" action="/route" method="POST" timeout="6">
    <Say>Press 1 for sales or 2 for support.</Say>
  </Gather>
  <Dial timeout="20">
    <Queue>support</Queue>
  </Dial>
  <Record maxLength="120" transcribe="true" action="/voicemail" />
</Response>{% endhighlight %}{% endset %}
			{%- set terminal = { label: "inbound.xml", pill: "VoiceML · 200 OK", code: code } %}
			{% include "partials/v2/terminal.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="call-control" aria-labelledby="call-control-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Call control</p>
				<h2 id="call-control-heading">Answer, route, record, gather, dial, queue, conference, redirect, stream, and transcribe.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Signed webhooks help your application verify callbacks, and existing handlers can be pointed toward VoiceTel when they stay within the supported VoiceML-compatible surface.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/voiceml/compatibility/">Compatibility matrix</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rows = [
					{ title: "Signed webhooks", meta: "verify every callback", state: "Signed" },
					{ title: "Existing handlers", meta: "point them at VoiceTel", state: "Unchanged", neutral: true },
					{ title: "English speech-to-text", meta: "free default from day one", state: "Included" },
					{ title: "Production STT, TTS, and storage", meta: "your preferred vendor, billed directly", state: "No markup" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/status-card.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3 class="subsection-heading">What developers can build</h3>
		{%- set featureHeading = "h4" %}
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "Inbound IVRs and call routing", body: "Create phone menus, route callers by input, forward to queues, record voicemails, and send callbacks into your application." },
			{ icon: "broadcast-pin", title: "Outbound calling workflows", body: "Trigger calls from your product, control call behavior with markup, and connect users, agents, customers, or automated systems." },
			{ icon: "record-circle", title: "Call recording and transcription", body: "Free defaults get you transcribing English calls on day one. Swap in your preferred STT, TTS, or recording-storage vendor when you're ready to tune for production &mdash; billed directly, no VoiceTel markup." },
			{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "Queues, conferences, live call control", body: "Build support, sales, dispatch, appointment, and contact-center workflows without starting from scratch." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="validator" aria-labelledby="validator-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Validator</p>
				<h2 id="validator-heading">Verify your markup before you ship.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Paste any VoiceML response into the validator and confirm every element is well-formed XML and matches the verb / noun schema. Pure client-side; nothing uploaded.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/voiceml/validator/">Open the validator</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set docs = [
					{ icon: "list-check", title: "VoiceML validator", meta: "schema check · client-side", href: "/voiceml/validator/" },
					{ icon: "layers", title: "Compatibility matrix", meta: "supported verbs and attributes", href: "/voiceml/compatibility/" },
					{ icon: "arrow-right-circle", title: "Migration guide", meta: "voiceml.voicetel.com", href: "/voiceml/migrate/" },
					{ icon: "book", title: "VoiceML overview", meta: "product page", href: "/voiceml/" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/docs-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Start building with VoiceTel.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Update your existing voice URL to <code>voiceml.voicetel.com</code> and your markup works unchanged.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/voiceml/migrate/">Migration guide</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
